---
# Every state has a keystroke left (Esc, Enter, typing): nothing here can
# deadlock, and the bounds (one queued message, one extra at a time) are
# rest, not a stuck page.
deadlock_detection: false
---

# Which handler wins a key while the person is typing in the web
# composer (web/src/app.tsx Thread's textarea onKeyDown and send();
# the window keydown handlers in App for ?, Cmd+P, Option+N, Option+I;
# palette.tsx usePaletteKey for Cmd+K; mention.tsx's capture handler for
# an open / or @ picker; keys.ts escStops, sheetKey, switchKey,
# newSessionKey, focusComposerKey; dialog.tsx for modal dialogs and the
# Keyboard shortcuts sheet).
#
# One session on screen, a Mac keyboard: Option+letter types a letter or
# starts a dead key (Option+N is the ~ of ñ, Option+I the ^ of î/ê).
#
# Fields (all on the Composer role):
#   turn      this session's turn: idle | sending (sent, not yet taken:
#             "Sending") | running | stopping (Esc pressed, the stop in
#             flight; the row still says running)
#   draft     "" | typed
#   queued    a Cmd+Enter message is waiting for the turn to end
#   overlay   what owns the keys besides the textarea: none | picker (the
#             / or @ caret picker) | dialog (a modal: a confirm, the
#             Start thread prompt) | sheet (Keyboard shortcuts) |
#             palette (Cmd+K / Cmd+P / Option+N quick access)
#   composing an IME composition is open in the textarea
#   focus     composer | page (focus left the textarea: the transcript, a
#             toolbar button). An open dialog, sheet or palette holds
#             focus itself; closing it puts focus back in the composer.
#   transcript ok | failed: the transcript did not load ("Transcript
#             didn't load", Retry)
#   acting    "" | here | elsewhere: an act() in flight (a model or
#             effort change, an archive) addressed to this session, or
#             to another one the person started it on before coming here
#   refused   "" | busy | load: the reason an Enter was refused, shown
#             by the composer until the cause clears
#   last      the keystroke that made this state, tracked by the adapter
#             (it pressed it): "" (not a key: a click, the server) |
#             print (a character or newline typed with focus in the
#             textarea: a letter, ?, Option+N, Option+I, Shift+Enter) |
#             enter | mod_enter | esc | shortcut (a key pressed outside
#             the textarea, or Cmd+P/Cmd+K anywhere)
#
# Derived in view():
#   send_enabled   the Send (Steer) button is enabled
#
# Where this departs from the code, and why (the spec says what the page
# must do; each of these is a finding for the MBT and browser stages):
# - ? into an empty composer: keys.ts sheetKey opens the shortcut sheet
#   and preventDefault swallows the ?. Here it lands in the draft; the
#   sheet opens only from outside a text field.
# - Option+N and Option+I are matched by e.code (keys.ts altCode) in a
#   window handler that runs for a textarea too: Option+N in the
#   composer opens the new-session palette instead of starting ñ, and
#   Option+I with focus already in the composer is preventDefault-ed, so
#   î and ê are lost. Here both type in the composer and act as
#   shortcuts only from outside it.
# - send() does not check failedLoad: the Send button is disabled while
#   the transcript failed to load, but Enter sends. Here Enter is
#   refused and says why.
# - busy is App-global (act() in app.tsx), and Thread gets busy={busy ||
#   locked[id]}: a model change in any session disables every
#   session's Send, and send() returns silently. Here only an act on
#   this session refuses Enter, and a refusal says why. (The queue
#   flush waits on the same global busy.)
# - Cmd+K (usePaletteKey) has no .dlg-scrim guard, unlike Cmd+P and
#   Option+N: over an open dialog it may open the palette. Here Cmd+P and
#   Cmd+K do nothing while a dialog or the sheet is open.
# Scope:
# - One extra at a time: a picker, dialog, sheet, palette, IME
#   composition, failed load, act in flight or focus away each start
#   only from a plain composer (plain() below), and cross only the turn
#   and the draft. Crossing them all is ~10x the states, every path one
#   browser test, and shows no new routing.
# - Enter inside a dialog, the sheet or the palette is theirs (confirm,
#   pick) and never reaches the composer: not modeled, Esc closes them.
# - Typing inside the palette's own input, the Stop button, the queue's
#   order, a stopped prompt put back and the steer/queue handshake are
#   stop_interrupt.fizz and steer_queue.fizz. A pick in a picker keeps
#   the draft "typed"; what it inserts is skills_mentions.fizz.
# - Alt+I off a Mac (no character) is the Option+I shortcut from the
#   page; it is not a separate action.

role Composer:
    action Init:
        self.turn = "idle"
        self.draft = ""
        self.queued = False
        self.overlay = "none"
        self.composing = False
        self.focus = "composer"
        self.transcript = "ok"
        self.acting = ""
        self.refused = ""
        self.last = ""
        self.view()

    atomic func view():
        self.send_enabled = self.draft != "" and self.transcript == "ok" and self.acting != "here"

    # The composer with nothing extra: see "One extra at a time".
    atomic func plain():
        return (self.overlay == "none" and not self.composing and self.focus == "composer"
                and self.transcript == "ok" and self.acting == "")

    # The textarea gets the key itself (no dialog, sheet or palette over
    # it). An open caret picker still lets the textarea have it.
    atomic func in_composer():
        return self.focus == "composer" and self.overlay in ["none", "picker"]

    # The row says running: stopping is still a running turn.
    atomic func running():
        return self.turn in ["running", "stopping"]

    # A send from the composer: what the Send button does, and nothing
    # the disabled button would not.
    atomic func send():
        if self.draft == "":
            return
        if self.transcript == "failed":
            self.refused = "load"
        elif self.acting == "here":
            self.refused = "busy"
        else:
            self.draft = ""
            self.refused = ""
            if self.turn == "idle":
                self.turn = "sending"

    # ---- typing in the composer ----

    # A letter (or anything printable that is not one of the keys
    # below). An open picker keeps filtering.
    atomic action Type:
        ic = self.in_composer()
        require ic and not self.composing
        self.draft = "typed"
        self.last = "print"
        self.view()

    # ? as a character, the draft empty or not.
    atomic action TypeQuestion:
        ic = self.in_composer()
        require ic and not self.composing
        self.draft = "typed"
        self.last = "print"
        self.view()

    # Option+N in the textarea: the ~ dead key (ñ).
    atomic action OptionN:
        ic = self.in_composer()
        require ic and not self.composing
        self.draft = "typed"
        self.last = "print"
        self.view()

    # Option+I in the textarea: the ^ dead key (î, ê).
    atomic action OptionI:
        ic = self.in_composer()
        require ic and not self.composing
        self.draft = "typed"
        self.last = "print"
        self.view()

    # A newline; it ends the / or @ token, so a picker shuts.
    atomic action ShiftEnter:
        ic = self.in_composer()
        require ic and not self.composing
        self.draft = "typed"
        self.overlay = "none"
        self.last = "print"
        self.view()

    # / at the start (or @ anywhere) opens the caret picker.
    atomic action Slash:
        pl = self.plain()
        require pl
        self.draft = "typed"
        self.overlay = "picker"
        self.last = "print"
        self.view()

    # An IME composition starts over a typed draft.
    atomic action Compose:
        pl = self.plain()
        require pl and self.draft != ""
        self.composing = True
        self.last = "print"
        self.view()

    # The Enter that confirms the composition: isComposing, never a send.
    atomic action ComposeEnd:
        require self.composing
        self.composing = False
        self.last = "enter"
        self.view()

    # ---- Enter, Cmd+Enter, Esc ----

    atomic action Enter:
        ic = self.in_composer()
        require ic and not self.composing
        self.last = "enter"
        if self.overlay == "picker":
            # The picker takes Enter (capture) and picks; nothing is sent.
            self.overlay = "none"
        else:
            self.send()
        self.view()

    # Cmd+Enter queues while the turn runs; otherwise it is Enter.
    atomic action ModEnter:
        ic = self.in_composer()
        require ic and not self.composing
        self.last = "mod_enter"
        if self.overlay == "picker":
            self.overlay = "none"
        elif self.turn in ["running", "stopping"]:
            if self.draft != "":
                self.draft = ""
                self.queued = True
        else:
            self.send()
        self.view()

    atomic action Esc:
        ic = self.in_composer()
        require ic or self.overlay in ["dialog", "sheet", "palette"]
        self.last = "esc"
        if self.overlay in ["dialog", "sheet", "palette"]:
            self.overlay = "none"
            self.focus = "composer"
        elif self.composing:
            self.composing = False
        elif self.overlay == "picker":
            self.overlay = "none"
        elif self.turn in ["sending", "running"]:
            self.turn = "stopping"
        self.view()

    # ---- shortcuts ----

    # Cmd+P (switch) and Cmd+K (all): from the textarea, a picker or the
    # page, never over a dialog or the sheet. Over the palette it stays.
    atomic action ModP:
        require not self.composing and self.overlay not in ["dialog", "sheet"]
        pl = self.plain()
        require self.focus == "page" or self.overlay == "palette" or pl or self.overlay == "picker"
        self.overlay = "palette"
        self.focus = "composer"
        self.last = "shortcut"
        self.view()

    atomic action ModK:
        require not self.composing and self.overlay not in ["dialog", "sheet"]
        pl = self.plain()
        require self.focus == "page" or self.overlay == "palette" or pl or self.overlay == "picker"
        self.overlay = "palette"
        self.focus = "composer"
        self.last = "shortcut"
        self.view()

    # From outside a text field: ? shows the sheet, Option+N the
    # new-session palette, Option+I goes into the composer.
    atomic action PageQuestion:
        require self.focus == "page" and self.overlay == "none"
        self.overlay = "sheet"
        self.focus = "composer"
        self.last = "shortcut"
        self.view()

    atomic action PageOptionN:
        require self.focus == "page" and self.overlay == "none"
        self.overlay = "palette"
        self.focus = "composer"
        self.last = "shortcut"
        self.view()

    atomic action PageOptionI:
        require self.focus == "page" and self.overlay == "none"
        self.focus = "composer"
        self.last = "shortcut"
        self.view()

    # ---- clicks and the rest of the page ----

    atomic action ClickPage:
        pl = self.plain()
        require pl
        self.focus = "page"
        self.last = ""
        self.view()

    # A modal dialog opens (the archive confirm, Start thread).
    atomic action OpenDialog:
        pl = self.plain()
        require pl
        self.overlay = "dialog"
        self.last = ""
        self.view()

    # A model pick in this session's toolbar: act() in flight here.
    atomic action ChangeModel:
        pl = self.plain()
        require pl
        self.acting = "here"
        self.last = ""
        self.view()

    # An act() the person started on another session is still in flight.
    atomic action ActElsewhere:
        pl = self.plain()
        require pl
        self.acting = "elsewhere"
        self.last = ""
        self.view()

    atomic fair action ActDone:
        require self.acting != ""
        self.acting = ""
        if self.refused == "busy":
            self.refused = ""
        self.last = ""
        self.view()

    atomic action LoadFails:
        pl = self.plain()
        require pl
        self.transcript = "failed"
        self.last = ""
        self.view()

    # The thread's Retry. Fair: the liveness below is about the page
    # once the person retries, not about a server that never answers.
    atomic fair action Reload:
        require self.transcript == "failed"
        self.transcript = "ok"
        if self.refused == "load":
            self.refused = ""
        self.last = ""
        self.view()

    # ---- the turn ----

    atomic fair action Taken:
        require self.turn == "sending"
        self.turn = "running"
        self.last = ""
        self.view()

    atomic action Finish:
        require self.turn == "running"
        self.turn = "idle"
        self.last = ""
        self.view()

    atomic fair action Stopped:
        require self.turn == "stopping"
        self.turn = "idle"
        self.last = ""
        self.view()

    # The queued message goes out once the turn has ended and nothing
    # of this session's holds it.
    atomic fair action Flush:
        require self.turn == "idle" and self.queued and self.acting != "here" and self.transcript == "ok"
        self.queued = False
        self.turn = "sending"
        self.last = ""
        self.view()

action Init:
    composer = Composer()

# ---- safety ----

# A printable character typed into the composer lands in the draft, and
# never opens the sheet or the palette instead.
always assertion PrintableLands:
    c = composer
    return c.last != "print" or (c.draft != "" and c.focus == "composer" and c.overlay in ["none", "picker"])

# Enter (or Cmd+Enter outside a running turn) never sends what the
# disabled Send button refuses. A send is the draft leaving the composer
# on Enter, or on Cmd+Enter when no turn runs (a running turn queues it).
transition assertion EnterNeverBeyondButton(before, after):
    b = before.composer
    a = after.composer
    queue = a.last == "mod_enter" and b.turn in ["running", "stopping"]
    sent = a.last in ["enter", "mod_enter"] and b.draft != "" and a.draft == "" and not queue
    return not sent or b.send_enabled

# An Enter the composer owns, on a typed draft, either sends or says why.
transition assertion RefusedEnterSaysWhy(before, after):
    b = before.composer
    a = after.composer
    owned = a.last == "enter" and b.overlay == "none" and b.focus == "composer" and not b.composing and b.draft != ""
    return not owned or a.draft == "" or a.refused != ""

# The reason on screen is the reason that holds now.
always assertion RefusalIsCurrent:
    c = composer
    return (c.refused != "busy" or c.acting == "here") and (c.refused != "load" or c.transcript == "failed")

# The Enter that ends an IME composition is the IME's: nothing is sent.
transition assertion ComposeEnterNeverSends(before, after):
    b = before.composer
    a = after.composer
    return not (b.composing and a.last == "enter") or (a.draft == b.draft and a.turn == b.turn)

# Esc stops the turn only when no picker, dialog, sheet, palette or IME
# owns it, and then it does.
transition assertion EscStopsOnlyWhenFree(before, after):
    b = before.composer
    a = after.composer
    free = b.overlay == "none" and not b.composing and b.focus == "composer" and b.turn in ["sending", "running"]
    stops = b.turn != "stopping" and a.turn == "stopping"
    return stops == (a.last == "esc" and free)

# Cmd+Enter queues only while the turn runs.
transition assertion QueueOnlyWhileRunning(before, after):
    b = before.composer
    a = after.composer
    return not (a.queued and not b.queued) or (a.last == "mod_enter" and b.turn in ["running", "stopping"])

# Cmd+P and Cmd+K never open the palette over a dialog or the sheet.
transition assertion PaletteNotOverModal(before, after):
    b = before.composer
    a = after.composer
    return not (a.overlay == "palette" and b.overlay != "palette") or b.overlay not in ["dialog", "sheet"]

# An act on another session never blocks this composer.
always assertion BusyElsewhereNeverBlocks:
    c = composer
    return c.acting == "here" or (c.refused != "busy" and (c.draft == "" or c.transcript != "ok" or c.send_enabled))

# ---- liveness ----

# A refused Enter becomes possible once the cause clears: the act ends,
# the transcript loads, and the refusal goes with them.
always eventually assertion RefusalClears:
    return composer.refused == ""

always eventually assertion SendNotHeld:
    return composer.acting != "here" and composer.transcript == "ok"
